## Eating habits

- eat **smaller meals**, more often
- avoid eating in the **3 to 4 hours before bed**
- notice which foods and drinks trigger your symptoms, such as coffee, alcohol, chocolate, tomatoes, and fatty or spicy foods

## At night

- raise the **head of your bed** by 10 to 20cm, using blocks under the legs, so your chest and head are higher than your waist
- sleeping on your left side may help

## Other tips

- lose weight, if you are overweight
- stop smoking
- wear loose clothes around your waist
- find ways to relax, as stress can make symptoms worse

## Support

**Guts UK** has information about reflux and other digestive conditions.
